/** @page mlreleasehistory ml Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section ml_3_0 ml Module Version 3.0

    Initial release, shipped with %Qore 3.0.

    - Native ML algorithms, preprocessing tools, feature engineering,
      and statistical functions:
      - @ref Qore::ML::IsolationForest "IsolationForest" — anomaly detection using isolation trees
      - @ref Qore::ML::LOF "LOF" — Local Outlier Factor density-based anomaly detection
      - @ref Qore::ML::DBSCAN "DBSCAN" — density-based clustering
      - @ref Qore::ML::KMeans "KMeans" — k-means clustering with online updates
      - @ref Qore::ML::GMM "GMM" — Gaussian Mixture Model probabilistic clustering
      - @ref Qore::ML::LinearRegression "LinearRegression" — ordinary least squares regression
      - @ref Qore::ML::HoltWinters "HoltWinters" — triple exponential smoothing forecasting
      - @ref Qore::ML::SeasonalDecomposition "SeasonalDecomposition" — time series decomposition
      - @ref Qore::ML::PCA "PCA" — principal component analysis
      - @ref Qore::ML::LogisticRegression "LogisticRegression" — binary and multiclass classification
      - @ref Qore::ML::KNN "KNN" — k-nearest neighbors for classification and regression
    - Data preprocessing:
      - @ref Qore::ML::StandardScaler "StandardScaler" — put fields on the same scale (zero mean, unit variance)
      - @ref Qore::ML::MinMaxScaler "MinMaxScaler" — normalize values to a configurable range (e.g., 0 to 1)
      - @ref Qore::ML::Imputer "Imputer" — fill missing values using average, median, most common, or fixed value
      - @ref Qore::ML::MLPipeline "MLPipeline" — chain preprocessing and analysis into a single fit/predict unit
    - Model evaluation:
      - Classification metrics: @ref Qore::ML::ml_accuracy() "ml_accuracy()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_confusion_matrix() "ml_confusion_matrix()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_classification_report() "ml_classification_report()"
      - Regression metrics: @ref Qore::ML::ml_mse() "ml_mse()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_rmse() "ml_rmse()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_mae() "ml_mae()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_r2_score() "ml_r2_score()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_explained_variance() "ml_explained_variance()"
      - Clustering metrics: @ref Qore::ML::ml_silhouette_score() "ml_silhouette_score()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_davies_bouldin_score() "ml_davies_bouldin_score()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_calinski_harabasz_score() "ml_calinski_harabasz_score()"
      - @ref Qore::ML::CrossValidator "CrossValidator" — k-fold cross-validation split utility
    - Optional @ref Qore::ML::OnnxModel "OnnxModel" for ONNX Runtime inference (requires libonnxruntime)
    - Typed model hierarchy under @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLModel "AbstractMLModel":
      - @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLEstimator "AbstractMLEstimator" — fit/predict-style models (regressors, classifiers, clusterers, anomaly detectors)
      - @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLRegressor "AbstractMLRegressor", @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLClassifier "AbstractMLClassifier",
        @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLClusterer "AbstractMLClusterer", @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLAnomalyDetector "AbstractMLAnomalyDetector"
      - @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLTransformer "AbstractMLTransformer" — fit/transform-style preprocessors
      - @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLTimeSeries "AbstractMLTimeSeries" — time-series forecasting models
      - All concrete model classes inherit from the appropriate base; ml_serialize / ml_deserialize / ml_save_model / ml_load_model
        accept any @ref Qore::ML::AbstractMLModel "AbstractMLModel" and route via virtual dispatch
    - Model persistence: @ref Qore::ML::ml_serialize() "ml_serialize()" / @ref Qore::ML::ml_deserialize() "ml_deserialize()" for in-memory round-trip,
      @ref Qore::ML::ml_save_model() "ml_save_model()" / @ref Qore::ML::ml_load_model() "ml_load_model()" for file-based persistence (.qml native format).
      @ref Qore::ML::MLPipeline "MLPipeline" composes through serialization: each step's state is packed by algorithm tag so a pipeline
      round-trips end-to-end and produces identical predictions after restore
    - Online learning (incremental updates) for KMeans, LinearRegression, GMM, and LogisticRegression
    - All algorithms use Eigen3 for efficient matrix operations
    - All algorithms support cooperative cancellation for responsive interrupt handling
    - \c NOTHING values in input data are treated as missing values for Imputer compatibility
    - @ref Qore::ML::ml_get_capabilities() "ml_get_capabilities()" function for runtime capability and ONNX support discovery
    - Tree-based algorithms:
      - @ref Qore::ML::DecisionTree "DecisionTree" — CART with Gini, entropy, and MSE criteria; feature importance
      - @ref Qore::ML::RandomForest "RandomForest" — bagging ensemble with bootstrap sampling and random feature subsets
      - @ref Qore::ML::GradientBoostedTrees "GradientBoostedTrees" — gradient boosting with log-loss and MSE; early stopping; row subsampling
      - Shared FlatTree CART engine with flat-array node storage
      - @ref Qore::ML::FeatureImportanceInfo "FeatureImportanceInfo" hashdecl for tree-based feature importance
    - Additional classifiers:
      - @ref Qore::ML::SVM "SVM" — support vector machine with simplified SMO, linear and RBF kernels, multiclass via one-vs-one voting
      - @ref Qore::ML::NaiveBayes "NaiveBayes" — Gaussian Naive Bayes with online learning (incremental mean/variance updates via Welford's algorithm)
    - Statistical functions:
      - Descriptive: @ref Qore::ML::ml_percentile() "ml_percentile()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_iqr() "ml_iqr()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_skewness() "ml_skewness()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_kurtosis() "ml_kurtosis()"
      - Correlation: @ref Qore::ML::ml_correlation_matrix() "ml_correlation_matrix()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_covariance_matrix() "ml_covariance_matrix()"
      - Hypothesis testing: @ref Qore::ML::ml_t_test() "ml_t_test()" (Welch's, exact p-values via Cephes incbet), @ref Qore::ML::ml_chi_squared_test() "ml_chi_squared_test()"
      - Normal distribution: @ref Qore::ML::ml_normal_pdf() "ml_normal_pdf()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_normal_cdf() "ml_normal_cdf()", @ref Qore::ML::ml_normal_ppf() "ml_normal_ppf()"
    - Feature engineering:
      - @ref Qore::ML::OneHotEncoder "OneHotEncoder" — categorical-to-binary column encoding with drop_first option
      - @ref Qore::ML::LabelEncoder "LabelEncoder" — string/integer-to-consecutive-integer mapping with inverse transform
      - @ref Qore::ML::VarianceThreshold "VarianceThreshold" — feature selector removing low-variance features (population variance)
      - @ref Qore::ML::PolynomialFeatures "PolynomialFeatures" — polynomial and interaction term generation with configurable degree
      - @ref Qore::ML::SelectKBest "SelectKBest" — top-k feature selection by ANOVA F-test or mutual information
      - @ref Qore::ML::RFE "RFE" — recursive feature elimination using decision tree importances
      - @ref Qore::ML::DateTimeFeatures "DateTimeFeatures" — extract numeric components (day_of_week, hour, quarter, is_weekend, etc.) from dates
      - @ref Qore::ML::TextFeatures "TextFeatures" — TF-IDF and bag-of-words text vectorization
    - Concept drift detection for monitoring deployed models:
      - @ref Qore::ML::ADWIN "ADWIN" — adaptive windowing with O(log N) memory
      - @ref Qore::ML::PageHinkley "PageHinkley" — cumulative sum test for mean shifts
      - @ref Qore::ML::DDM "DDM" — error rate monitoring with warning and drift levels
    - Vector similarity functions for embedding/RAG pipelines:
      - @ref Qore::ML::ml_cosine_similarity() "ml_cosine_similarity()" — direction similarity (-1 to 1)
      - @ref Qore::ML::ml_dot_product() "ml_dot_product()" — element-wise product sum
      - @ref Qore::ML::ml_euclidean_distance() "ml_euclidean_distance()" — straight-line distance
      - @ref Qore::ML::ml_manhattan_distance() "ml_manhattan_distance()" — city-block distance
    - Added @ref Qore::ML::Tensor "Tensor" and
      @ref Qore::ML::OnnxModel::runTensors() "OnnxModel::runTensors()" for dense
      ONNX inference with \c buffer<T> storage and explicit shape metadata
    - @ref Qore::ML::OnnxModel::run() "OnnxModel::run()",
      @ref Qore::ML::OnnxModel::runTensors() "OnnxModel::runTensors()",
      @ref Qore::ML::OnnxModel::runBatch() "OnnxModel::runBatch()", and the
      synchronous @ref Qore::ML::OnnxSessionPool "OnnxSessionPool" inference
      methods can request selected ONNX output tensors by name, avoiding
      unnecessary materialization for multi-output models
    - Added @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::fromColumns() "Tensor::fromColumns()" to
      pack equal-length dense column buffers into a row-major tensor without
      row hash or nested list materialization
    - Added @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::reshape() "Tensor::reshape()",
      @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::sliceRows() "Tensor::sliceRows()", and
      @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::concatRows() "Tensor::concatRows()" for
      zero-copy tensor reshaping, row slicing, and native batch assembly
    - Added @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::sigmoid() "Tensor::sigmoid()",
      @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::softmax() "Tensor::softmax()",
      @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::argmax() "Tensor::argmax()",
      @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::topK() "Tensor::topK()",
      @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::poolTokenEmbeddings() "Tensor::poolTokenEmbeddings()",
      and @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::l2NormalizeRows() "Tensor::l2NormalizeRows()"
      for dense ONNX postprocessing without nested list materialization
    - Added @ref Qore::ML::Tensor::toColumnBuffers() "Tensor::toColumnBuffers()"
      to split rank-1 and rank-2 tensor outputs into dense column buffers for
      DataFrame and DataProvider pipelines
    - ONNX tensor conversion supports float, double, int8, int16, int32,
      int64, and bool inputs and outputs
*/
